                "reply_count": 13,
                "retweet_count": 5,
                "source": "Twitter Web App",
                "text": "Hemp-derived intoxicants like Delta-8 THC pose serious public health risks. Between 2021 and February 2025, U.S. poison control centers handled 10,263 cases involving Delta-8 THC exposures. Even more troubling, these products are often marketed in ways that appeal directly to children. I personally confronted the General Counsel of the Hemp Roundtable for their continued support of companies that sell and promote addictive hemp products to children. Candy-like items such as Triple Strength THC Watermelon Lemonade Space Chews have no place on the market and should be banned outright.\n\n@GOPoversight",
                "text_lang": "en",
